1
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:15,476
MISSION
CAPTURE THE MASTERMIND.

2
00:00:17,506 --> 00:00:19,383
MISSION
COMMIT MURDER.

3
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:23,387
MISSION   CLEAR THE CHECKPOINTS WITHIN
THE TIME LIMITS AND REACH THE GOAL.

4
00:00:25,515 --> 00:00:27,391
MISSION

5
00:00:29,519 --> 00:00:31,395
MISSION

6
00:00:32,831 --> 00:00:34,916
5 CONTESTANTS LEFT.

7
00:00:34,941 --> 00:00:39,570
7 DAYS AND 4 HOURS UNTIL THE GAME ENDS.

8
00:00:43,156 --> 00:00:47,009
TOKYO
PM 03:02 JST

9
00:00:51,494 --> 00:00:52,247
Yes?

10
00:00:53,162 --> 00:00:57,792
The body of Dao Saetang,
who was kidnapped in Bangkok,

11
00:00:57,917 --> 00:01:00,002
has been discovered.

12
00:01:00,298 --> 00:01:02,056
Another person was killed.

13
00:01:03,506 --> 00:01:07,556
I don't know what I should be doing
at a time like this.

14
00:01:08,219 --> 00:01:11,097
I don't know if this is right either.

15
00:01:12,139 --> 00:01:16,852
But I know that Saori would say this...

16
00:01:18,979 --> 00:01:20,648
"Rescue everyone."

17
00:01:34,662 --> 00:01:38,833
As long as the game continues,
there will be casualties.

18
00:01:41,001 --> 00:01:43,681
If one person succeeds, the rest will die.

19
00:01:46,131 --> 00:01:50,584
It's a sick, twisted game...

20
00:01:56,642 --> 00:01:59,816
-That's why I'm going to Seoul.
-Seoul?

21
00:02:01,605 --> 00:02:04,191
The player there is in a bad situation.

22
00:02:04,442 --> 00:02:08,929
Seoul... You're meeting the girl's father,
Han Kiju the doctor, right?

23
00:02:09,804 --> 00:02:10,875
Yeah.

24
00:02:11,866 --> 00:02:13,367
SEOUL

25
00:02:13,492 --> 00:02:16,203
PM 03:10 KST

26
00:02:17,413 --> 00:02:20,791
I WILL SOLVE THIS CASE AND SAVE EVERYONE
MIXED UP IN IT. INCLUDING YOU.

27
00:02:23,753 --> 00:02:26,297
Including me...?

28
00:02:29,049 --> 00:02:30,801
He's not replying!

29
00:02:32,219 --> 00:02:34,013
-Replying?
-Look!

30
00:02:40,352 --> 00:02:44,106
It's nothing. Just enjoy your meal.

31
00:02:53,032 --> 00:02:54,700
I told you, it's a prank.

32
00:02:54,825 --> 00:02:57,328
People are being killed!

33
00:03:01,916 --> 00:03:02,833
Keep it down.

34
00:03:02,958 --> 00:03:07,463
Everyone's saying they were killed
in the kiDnap GAME!

35
00:03:07,838 --> 00:03:10,925
Another kiDnap GAME death.

36
00:03:11,884 --> 00:03:13,427
What's going on?

37
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:21,727
Did he reply to you?

38
00:03:23,771 --> 00:03:24,980
-Show me.
-Calm down.

39
00:03:25,189 --> 00:03:27,525
Show me! Give it to me!

40
00:03:27,650 --> 00:03:30,486
-I have to get to Rian!
-Let go!

41
00:03:30,653 --> 00:03:32,029
Ayun! Stop!

42
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,534
Ayun?! You all right?

43
00:03:46,252 --> 00:03:47,461
Murderer...

44
00:03:49,713 --> 00:03:54,593
You robbed Rian of her sight.

45
00:03:57,596 --> 00:03:59,682
Now you're leaving her to die.

46
00:04:18,325 --> 00:04:20,035
I'm being forced to play.

47
00:04:25,916 --> 00:04:28,544
YOU HAVE BEEN ENLISTED IN THE
KIDNAP GAME.

48
00:04:29,211 --> 00:04:30,546
My mission...

49
00:04:32,423 --> 00:04:34,383
is to commit murder.

50
00:05:09,209 --> 00:05:12,755
KIDNAP GAME

51
00:05:15,716 --> 00:05:17,676
"Commit murder"?

52
00:05:19,678 --> 00:05:20,721
Yes.

53
00:05:23,182 --> 00:05:28,103
If you kill someone, will that save Rian?

54
00:05:31,148 --> 00:05:34,950
It fulfils the mission, so yes.

55
00:05:41,742 --> 00:05:44,828
Rian's going to be all right, isn't she?

56
00:05:48,207 --> 00:05:51,210
You'll kill someone to save her, right?

57
00:05:55,089 --> 00:05:56,548
You're her father!

58
00:05:57,383 --> 00:05:59,885
Rian was kidnapped in front of you!

59
00:06:01,929 --> 00:06:03,514
Why hesitate?!

60
00:06:03,639 --> 00:06:06,016
Whatever it takes, do it!

61
00:06:11,146 --> 00:06:15,234
Would you be able to kill someone
if they told you to?

62
00:06:15,359 --> 00:06:16,694
I would.

63
00:06:20,114 --> 00:06:21,198
What?

64
00:06:21,323 --> 00:06:24,576
I'd do anything for her.
I'm her parent.

65
00:06:24,702 --> 00:06:28,580
Rian's my child.
I'd even commit murder...

66
00:06:48,350 --> 00:06:51,270
The person I admire the most is my dad.

67
00:06:51,353 --> 00:06:51,895
5 YEARS AGO

68
00:06:51,895 --> 00:06:54,189
He is a doctor.

69
00:06:54,314 --> 00:06:58,235
My dad's job is saving people's lives.

70
00:06:58,736 --> 00:07:03,532
I want to become someone who can
save people, just like him.

71
00:07:09,788 --> 00:07:14,126
It's thanks to you that she's grown
to be such a good girl.

72
00:07:15,085 --> 00:07:20,174
It's a nice memory to have
before I leave Seoul.

73
00:07:20,716 --> 00:07:24,011
Call Rian from Japan from time to time, okay?

74
00:07:24,136 --> 00:07:27,431
I'll call every day. If there's time.

75
00:07:29,349 --> 00:07:31,977
You know...

76
00:07:32,603 --> 00:07:38,192
Lately Rian's been saying from time to time
that her eyes get blurry.

77
00:07:39,109 --> 00:07:42,905
I'll talk to the hospital.
Have them run some tests.

78
00:07:45,741 --> 00:07:48,452
TOKYO GENERAL MEDICAL CENTER

79
00:07:48,786 --> 00:07:50,537
A brain tumor?!

80
00:07:52,915 --> 00:07:56,543
She might not only go blind.
She may even die.

81
00:07:57,628 --> 00:07:59,129
No...

82
00:07:59,254 --> 00:08:03,175
Please, you have to save her!

83
00:08:03,675 --> 00:08:10,182
Yes, of course. I'll return to Seoul at once.
I'll make sure she pulls through this.

84
00:08:10,516 --> 00:08:13,227
OPERATING CENTER

85
00:08:14,103 --> 00:08:16,688
It's right behind the optic nerve.

86
00:08:35,415 --> 00:08:37,751
Will she go blind?

87
00:08:39,336 --> 00:08:41,296
You said it would succeed...

88
00:08:45,884 --> 00:08:48,136
That you'd fix her eyes...

89
00:09:00,482 --> 00:09:04,486
Dad, did you quit being a doctor?

90
00:09:04,611 --> 00:09:05,696
2 YEARS AGO

91
00:09:06,029 --> 00:09:08,157
No, I didn't quit.

92
00:09:09,491 --> 00:09:13,245
But you're at home all the time now.

93
00:09:15,247 --> 00:09:17,040
Ah, you see,

94
00:09:17,332 --> 00:09:23,964
I work part-time,
only when the hospital needs me.

95
00:09:24,882 --> 00:09:26,300
I'm glad.

96
00:09:29,177 --> 00:09:34,663
I love how you're a doctor who saves people.

97
00:09:40,564 --> 00:09:41,899
Is that right?

98
00:09:59,583 --> 00:10:03,128
I WILL SOLVE THIS CASE AND SAVE
EVERYONE MIXED UP IN IT.

99
00:10:03,253 --> 00:10:06,173
INCLUDING YOU.

100
00:10:13,096 --> 00:10:17,434
SHINJUKU CENTRAL POLICE STATION

101
00:10:18,769 --> 00:10:21,150
-Get in.
-Akina? Where are we going?

102
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:23,482
-Just c'mon.
-Okay.

103
00:10:24,650 --> 00:10:25,430
Excuse me.

104
00:10:30,072 --> 00:10:32,908
Niide asked me to contact you.

105
00:10:33,033 --> 00:10:34,368
Niide?!

106
00:10:35,202 --> 00:10:38,872
But I've been suspended for two weeks.

107
00:10:39,289 --> 00:10:42,751
He predicted that was going to happen.

108
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:44,378
What do you mean?

109
00:10:44,753 --> 00:10:49,049
Niide has to capture the Mastermind.
Without the police.

110
00:10:49,174 --> 00:10:52,219
Technically,
you're not a police officer on duty.

111
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:03,480
TEITO TELEVISION

112
00:11:04,106 --> 00:11:06,233
Niide wants you to find him.

113
00:11:07,484 --> 00:11:10,779
-Who is he?
-He's involved in the kidnappings.

114
00:11:10,904 --> 00:11:14,533
He was there during
the bomb scare at the hospital.

115
00:11:14,658 --> 00:11:17,170
The firecrackers incident Niide was at?

116
00:11:19,288 --> 00:11:22,476
Everything we know so far is in here.

117
00:11:25,752 --> 00:11:29,381
All right. By the way, where's Niide?

118
00:11:29,506 --> 00:11:32,092
-Off to Seoul.
-Seoul?

119
00:11:32,938 --> 00:11:36,656
A doctor there is planning a murder
to complete his mission.

120
00:11:37,264 --> 00:11:38,724
Niide's gone to look for him.

121
00:11:38,849 --> 00:11:43,311
Wait, so he's going to the airport?!
That's a bad idea.

122
00:11:43,645 --> 00:11:46,982
The SIT is there.
Inspector Samejima set a trap.

123
00:11:49,401 --> 00:11:52,279
That's why Niide's gone to Fukuoka.

124
00:11:53,363 --> 00:11:55,157
-Fukuoka?
-The Busan ferry.

125
00:11:55,907 --> 00:12:00,746
It's a detour,
but chances are it's off their radar.

126
00:12:03,689 --> 00:12:07,264
A QUIET LIFE
AFTER HANGING UP THE SCALPEL

127
00:12:08,003 --> 00:12:12,007
I will complete my mission
and save Rian by any means possible.

128
00:13:03,350 --> 00:13:04,357
Why hesitate?!

129
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:07,729
Whatever it takes, do it!

130
00:13:28,667 --> 00:13:30,001
I'm sorry...

131
00:13:34,381 --> 00:13:35,549
I'm so...

132
00:13:54,776 --> 00:13:55,423
Dr. Han?

133
00:14:00,657 --> 00:14:01,491
Oh, hello.

134
00:14:02,451 --> 00:14:03,535
What are you doing?

135
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:06,991
I, uh...

136
00:14:08,039 --> 00:14:11,096
I know this patient.
I came to see how she's doing.

137
00:14:12,169 --> 00:14:14,983
What about you?

138
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:23,555
There's an operation scheduled for tomorrow,
but the surgeon came down with a fever.

139
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:27,767
Trying to find a replacement
but nobody's available.

140
00:14:28,602 --> 00:14:29,656
Is that so?

141
00:14:31,229 --> 00:14:33,470
I'm sorry that I can't help.

142
00:14:56,046 --> 00:15:01,051
DANGER: HIGH-CONCENTRATION DRUG

143
00:15:37,087 --> 00:15:38,922
-Come on.
-Let me go!

144
00:15:39,047 --> 00:15:42,133
Come here!

145
00:15:42,592 --> 00:15:43,802
Whiskey highball.

146
00:15:45,554 --> 00:15:46,721
You're hurting me!

147
00:15:46,846 --> 00:15:49,599
Let's drink somewhere else, just us.

148
00:15:49,724 --> 00:15:52,602
I'm not interested. Get lost, asshole.

149
00:15:52,727 --> 00:15:54,187
What a charmer.

150
00:15:54,312 --> 00:15:57,315
Were you leading me on just now or what?

151
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,483
-Me?
-Yeah, you!

152
00:15:58,542 --> 00:16:01,086
-When was I leading you on?
-Just now.

153
00:16:04,155 --> 00:16:07,450
-Stay put. I'm talking to you.
-That hurts!

154
00:16:07,576 --> 00:16:09,869
Come off it. Stay put.

155
00:16:09,995 --> 00:16:11,246
Let go.

156
00:16:11,830 --> 00:16:14,791
-No. Let's talk outside.
-Talk about what?!

157
00:16:18,169 --> 00:16:19,754
I'd even commit murder...

158
00:16:20,130 --> 00:16:21,881
I wanna talk to you.

159
00:16:22,173 --> 00:16:25,383
-About what?
-You'll find out if you listen.

160
00:16:25,469 --> 00:16:28,356
-Why should I?
-I wanna talk.

161
00:16:28,471 --> 00:16:30,181
Let go, you creep!

162
00:16:31,576 --> 00:16:33,496
Bitch!

163
00:16:59,462 --> 00:17:00,880
What the hell?!

164
00:17:02,974 --> 00:17:04,355
Get back here!

165
00:17:27,697 --> 00:17:29,407
I can't do it.

166
00:17:57,769 --> 00:17:59,436
What am I supposed to do?!

167
00:18:02,482 --> 00:18:04,976
What am I supposed to do?!

168
00:18:19,541 --> 00:18:20,821
Are you trying to kill someone?

169
00:18:30,677 --> 00:18:34,390
The kiDnap GAME.
Is your mission "murder"?

170
00:18:41,730 --> 00:18:47,193
You're with them, aren't you!

171
00:18:47,318 --> 00:18:50,613
Give her back! Give Rian back!

172
00:18:54,117 --> 00:18:59,297
You want murder? You got it!

173
00:19:01,332 --> 00:19:03,916
You mustn't...
I'm not the kidnapper.

174
00:19:18,349 --> 00:19:23,688
Then why do you appear around me?
Why do you follow me around?

175
00:19:25,064 --> 00:19:26,711
I'm worried about you.

176
00:19:28,359 --> 00:19:29,778
Seven years ago,

177
00:19:30,528 --> 00:19:32,766
you saved my brother.

178
00:19:36,326 --> 00:19:38,661
He was a worthless vagrant,

179
00:19:40,955 --> 00:19:44,000
lying in the gutter.

180
00:19:45,335 --> 00:19:47,754
Yet you did everything to save him.

181
00:19:51,216 --> 00:19:52,592
I don't remember.

182
00:19:52,717 --> 00:19:54,928
To you, saving a life is normal.

183
00:19:56,429 --> 00:20:00,036
Which is why for you, murder is impossible.

184
00:20:13,947 --> 00:20:17,230
Then what?! What am I supposed to do?

185
00:20:20,411 --> 00:20:21,830
There's no other way!

186
00:20:25,375 --> 00:20:26,188
No other way...

187
00:20:39,722 --> 00:20:40,890
Doctor...

188
00:21:03,788 --> 00:21:04,803
Long day?

189
00:21:06,583 --> 00:21:08,949
Work.

190
00:21:11,588 --> 00:21:14,016
I was worried.
You left work a while ago.

191
00:21:14,882 --> 00:21:17,903
It took you a long time to get home.

192
00:21:20,638 --> 00:21:21,830
What are you worried about?

193
00:21:24,183 --> 00:21:25,727
The kiDnap GAME.

194
00:21:28,271 --> 00:21:30,064
Haven't you heard of it?

195
00:21:33,234 --> 00:21:34,777
It's just a rumor.

196
00:21:35,653 --> 00:21:37,223
If it were true,

197
00:21:38,072 --> 00:21:42,403
then you or your wife would also be
in that game, wouldn't you?

198
00:21:45,288 --> 00:21:47,540
If I were in the game,

199
00:21:47,916 --> 00:21:51,127
I wouldn't be drinking here, would I?!

200
00:21:51,544 --> 00:21:52,879
Kiju.

201
00:21:55,965 --> 00:21:57,483
You need to rest, dear.

202
00:22:00,094 --> 00:22:01,636
Good night.

203
00:22:18,237 --> 00:22:19,496
Weren't you able to do it?

204
00:22:23,076 --> 00:22:24,327
No. Sorry.

205
00:22:31,501 --> 00:22:32,794
Kill me.

206
00:22:34,253 --> 00:22:35,171
What?

207
00:22:35,630 --> 00:22:37,583
Isn't your mission to kill?

208
00:22:40,635 --> 00:22:43,054
Are you crazy? I can't kill you.

209
00:22:43,763 --> 00:22:45,807
Kill me... Just kill me!

210
00:22:47,892 --> 00:22:49,060
No!

211
00:22:52,230 --> 00:22:53,773
So...

212
00:22:56,693 --> 00:22:58,611
You're going to let Rian die?

213
00:23:00,697 --> 00:23:02,615
Someone has to die.

214
00:23:03,825 --> 00:23:05,743
You have a choice.

215
00:23:07,078 --> 00:23:09,247
Does Rian die?

216
00:23:10,157 --> 00:23:11,002
Do I die?

217
00:23:12,166 --> 00:23:13,263
Or does a stranger die?

218
00:23:21,884 --> 00:23:23,396
There's no need to kill you.

219
00:23:27,223 --> 00:23:28,156
I've made up my mind.

220
00:23:30,116 --> 00:23:34,170
I'll operate tomorrow.

221
00:23:44,032 --> 00:23:45,949
I put down my scalpel...

222
00:23:51,164 --> 00:23:52,523
because of these hands.

223
00:23:55,585 --> 00:23:59,743
When I stand at the operating table,
my fingers start to shake...

224
00:24:03,634 --> 00:24:04,876
I'm scared I'll mess up...

225
00:24:08,008 --> 00:24:08,996
Like with Rian...

226
00:24:12,310 --> 00:24:13,896
That operation was a success.

227
00:24:19,233 --> 00:24:19,856
But...

228
00:24:22,612 --> 00:24:25,870
Rian lost her sight.

229
00:24:26,991 --> 00:24:29,703
I took the light from her world.

230
00:24:32,997 --> 00:24:39,523
I failed the one person
I had to save over anyone else.

231
00:24:55,978 --> 00:25:01,651
Tomorrow, my hands are sure to shake...

232
00:25:04,987 --> 00:25:06,948
The surgery will fail.

233
00:25:10,576 --> 00:25:12,912
Because of me...

234
00:25:20,336 --> 00:25:25,550
The patient will die.

235
00:25:34,350 --> 00:25:37,603
KIDNAP GAME
DAY 4

236
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:43,550
AM 08:07 JST

237
00:25:46,445 --> 00:25:48,573
WHAT DOES THIS MEAN?

238
00:25:48,698 --> 00:25:54,495
I’LL HELP YOU IF YOU CAN SOLVE IT.
I THINK IT’S A PLACE IN SINGAPORE…

239
00:25:54,579 --> 00:25:55,288
SINGAPORE

240
00:25:55,329 --> 00:25:58,040
25 250...

241
00:25:58,416 --> 00:26:01,303
What is this? I don’t get it...

242
00:26:02,420 --> 00:26:05,990
25 250...

243
00:26:08,197 --> 00:26:12,118
Oh, no. Only three hours left...

244
00:26:19,437 --> 00:26:22,773
"Isn’t that the treetop walk
at MacRitchie Reservoir?

245
00:26:22,899 --> 00:26:28,362
"It’s a suspension bridge
25m high and 250m long."

246
00:26:29,822 --> 00:26:32,199
Yes! That must be it!

247
00:26:33,910 --> 00:26:36,370
Sorry, sorry, sorry...

248
00:26:37,747 --> 00:26:41,667
Hi! Wait! I'm coming!

249
00:26:41,792 --> 00:26:45,046
Oh my God! Wait for me, wait for me!

250
00:27:02,413 --> 00:27:05,930
SHOULD YOU REALLY BE HELPING ME?
WE’RE ENEMIES.

251
00:27:05,983 --> 00:27:09,320
CONSIDERING THE DIFFICULTY OF THE OTHER MISSIONS,
I EXPECT THAT YOU WILL MAKE SOME PROGRESS

252
00:27:09,362 --> 00:27:10,863
BUT NOT ENOUGH TO COMPLETE YOUR MISSION.

253
00:27:15,576 --> 00:27:20,456
THE KIDNAPPER IS JUST TOYING WITH YOU.
PLEASE WORK WITH ME.

254
00:27:36,013 --> 00:27:39,809
SORRY, BUT I’M GOING TO PRIORITIZE
WINNING THE GAME FOR MYSELF.

255
00:27:47,108 --> 00:27:51,612
I’M GRATEFUL FOR YOUR HELP.
SORRY FOR TRICKING YOU

256
00:27:59,245 --> 00:28:03,207
LET ME KNOW IF YOU CHANGE YOUR MIND.

257
00:28:19,724 --> 00:28:24,603
Thank you, doctor. Thank you so much
for agreeing to operate.

258
00:28:25,271 --> 00:28:27,815
I'll do my best.

259
00:28:29,358 --> 00:28:31,027
Thank you.

260
00:28:45,541 --> 00:28:48,502
I'm Han Kiju.
I'll be your surgeon today.

261
00:28:49,253 --> 00:28:51,005
Thank you, Doctor.

262
00:28:51,380 --> 00:28:55,968
Could you, please...
please save my father.

263
00:28:57,261 --> 00:28:59,680
I'll do my best.

264
00:29:01,072 --> 00:29:04,354
PM 12:36 KST

265
00:29:09,482 --> 00:29:11,067
Excuse me.

266
00:29:28,709 --> 00:29:31,363
-Hello, doctor.
-Hello.

267
00:29:40,888 --> 00:29:45,309
I'll be performing decompression surgery
on a recurrent brain tumor.

268
00:29:57,029 --> 00:30:00,908
Removing the portion
invading the brain tissue.

269
00:30:08,874 --> 00:30:10,668
MISSION
COMMIT MURDER.

270
00:30:19,677 --> 00:30:21,178
Doctor?

271
00:30:30,104 --> 00:30:31,897
Because of me...

272
00:30:34,817 --> 00:30:36,402
Is everything okay?

273
00:30:37,570 --> 00:30:38,612
The patient will die.

274
00:30:38,946 --> 00:30:41,365
Please... please save my father.

275
00:30:48,372 --> 00:30:52,042
My dad's job is saving people's lives.

276
00:30:52,543 --> 00:30:57,006
I want to become someone who can
save people, just like him.

277
00:31:00,718 --> 00:31:06,474
I love how you're a doctor who saves people.

278
00:31:55,856 --> 00:31:58,692
-Thank you so much!
-Thank you, sir.

279
00:32:28,097 --> 00:32:33,519
WOULD TAKING MY OWN LIFE FULFILL MY MISSION?

280
00:32:59,295 --> 00:33:02,006
PM 06:17 KST

281
00:33:12,766 --> 00:33:13,809
Excuse me. Sorry.

282
00:33:14,935 --> 00:33:17,438
Dr. Han, does he work here?

283
00:33:17,730 --> 00:33:20,399
Sorry, could you say that again?

284
00:33:20,524 --> 00:33:21,942
Doctor... Dr. Han.

285
00:33:23,736 --> 00:33:25,237
Ah, Director!

286
00:33:26,405 --> 00:33:30,784
Excuse me. I'm looking for Dr. Han Kiju.

287
00:33:30,909 --> 00:33:33,370
Are you a friend of Dr. Han?

288
00:33:33,495 --> 00:33:36,081
I'm with the Tokyo Metropolitan Police.

289
00:33:36,206 --> 00:33:42,087
I need to talk to Doctor Han Kiju
about the kidnapping.

290
00:33:42,212 --> 00:33:45,466
Oh, Dr. Han just finished an operation and left.

291
00:33:46,258 --> 00:33:47,593
An operation?

292
00:33:47,718 --> 00:33:52,890
Yeah. It was a very difficult operation.
But Dr. Han worked a miracle.

293
00:33:55,017 --> 00:33:56,644
The patient... survived?

294
00:33:56,769 --> 00:34:00,189
He did well despite the difficult situation.

295
00:34:01,106 --> 00:34:05,110
I will complete my mission and save Rian
by any means possible.

296
00:34:06,654 --> 00:34:09,531
But it looks like it took a toll on him.

297
00:34:09,782 --> 00:34:13,494
He just left with a very tired look on his face.

298
00:34:15,037 --> 00:34:17,164
All right, thank you.

299
00:34:29,968 --> 00:34:32,221
RIAN
RE: KIDNAP GAME

300
00:34:32,346 --> 00:34:35,891
YES.

301
00:34:50,739 --> 00:34:52,116
Dammit.

302
00:35:06,422 --> 00:35:07,256
You're her father!

303
00:35:07,840 --> 00:35:10,426
Rian was kidnapped in front of you!

304
00:36:40,974 --> 00:36:44,394
TAKE CARE OF RIAN FOR ME.

305
00:36:48,315 --> 00:36:50,567
You know, I can see it.

306
00:36:51,193 --> 00:36:55,489
No matter where, no matter when,
I can see your smile, Dad.

307
00:37:13,423 --> 00:37:14,800
Don't do it!

308
00:37:20,180 --> 00:37:23,350
-Who the hell are you?! Let me go!
-Calm down!

309
00:37:23,475 --> 00:37:25,394
Let me go!

310
00:37:31,650 --> 00:37:32,943
No!

311
00:37:34,278 --> 00:37:35,737
Let me go!

312
00:37:35,863 --> 00:37:37,948
I'm saving my daughter!

313
00:37:54,131 --> 00:37:57,634
You stay out of this!

314
00:37:57,843 --> 00:37:59,886
I'll kill you!

315
00:38:05,934 --> 00:38:07,394
Then do it!

316
00:38:08,937 --> 00:38:12,107
You can't! You can't kill anyone.

317
00:38:14,499 --> 00:38:16,000
It's not who you are!

318
00:38:17,140 --> 00:38:19,083
I have to save my daughter!

319
00:38:20,856 --> 00:38:25,662
I have to save her!

320
00:39:03,992 --> 00:39:08,288
I'm going to die and end this game...

321
00:39:08,956 --> 00:39:10,749
It's the only way.

322
00:39:11,249 --> 00:39:13,335
I can't let you do that.

323
00:39:16,254 --> 00:39:21,426
I'm part of this game, too.

324
00:39:25,555 --> 00:39:32,003
You just want to save your loved one, too.

325
00:39:33,855 --> 00:39:35,196
Sure, I want to save her.

326
00:39:37,651 --> 00:39:42,447
But Saori, my wife, she'd say...

327
00:39:45,742 --> 00:39:51,335
"It's not right to let someone like you
die for a game like this."

328
00:40:01,508 --> 00:40:07,355
You always fought for people's lives,

329
00:40:11,018 --> 00:40:13,103
even if it seemed hopeless.

330
00:40:15,439 --> 00:40:19,443
Even today, you saved someone.

331
00:40:26,408 --> 00:40:27,534
No.

332
00:40:30,954 --> 00:40:35,792
I tried to kill him and failed.

333
00:40:35,917 --> 00:40:37,419
That's not true!

334
00:40:40,422 --> 00:40:46,910
You understand more than anyone
how precious life is.

335
00:40:50,849 --> 00:40:58,729
That's why you're staking
your own life to save your daughter.

336
00:41:04,654 --> 00:41:10,577
You're fighting for her without
hurting or killing anybody.

337
00:41:17,417 --> 00:41:23,465
Do you want to prevail in this sick game?

338
00:41:32,849 --> 00:41:35,685
If one prevails...

339
00:41:39,856 --> 00:41:42,317
all the other lives are taken.

340
00:41:44,319 --> 00:41:46,696
Can you accept that?!

341
00:42:01,545 --> 00:42:04,963
I don't want any more people to die.

342
00:42:10,136 --> 00:42:11,555
Including my wife...

343
00:42:16,393 --> 00:42:18,145
and your daughter.

344
00:42:28,405 --> 00:42:29,739
I promise you...

345
00:42:31,992 --> 00:42:34,839
I'll save your daughter.
I'll save everyone.

346
00:42:36,163 --> 00:42:36,696
But...

347
00:42:40,959 --> 00:42:42,203
I need your help.

348
00:42:56,558 --> 00:42:58,023
Are you trying to save them

349
00:42:59,936 --> 00:43:01,390
because you're a detective?

350
00:43:07,235 --> 00:43:09,112
Do you save people

351
00:43:11,364 --> 00:43:13,241
because you're a doctor?

352
00:43:17,787 --> 00:43:19,122
That's not why.

353
00:43:51,529 --> 00:43:52,864
Thanks.

354
00:43:55,492 --> 00:43:58,323
You speak Japanese.

355
00:44:01,373 --> 00:44:03,363
I worked in Japan for a while.

356
00:44:06,044 --> 00:44:07,295
I see.

357
00:44:10,715 --> 00:44:13,260
-Which part...
-How will you save everyone?

358
00:44:16,429 --> 00:44:17,931
I don't know.

359
00:44:19,849 --> 00:44:24,609
That's why I need information
to track down the mastermind.

360
00:44:27,440 --> 00:44:32,445
Nothing comes to mind.

361
00:44:35,282 --> 00:44:37,200
Any information would help.

362
00:44:40,578 --> 00:44:41,830
Do you know him?

363
00:44:42,747 --> 00:44:45,476
He was in Japan, but spoke Korean.

364
00:44:50,338 --> 00:44:51,548
No.

365
00:44:53,633 --> 00:44:55,176
Okay...

366
00:44:59,097 --> 00:45:05,270
But there must be common factors
linking you, me, and the other players.

367
00:45:08,606 --> 00:45:12,235
Sorry... I'm not going to be much use.

368
00:45:12,360 --> 00:45:17,991
It's fine. I still need your help.
I can trust you.

369
00:45:26,875 --> 00:45:34,007
I failed my family and I failed my patients.

370
00:45:39,929 --> 00:45:43,600
I've failed as a husband
and a police officer...

371
00:45:47,354 --> 00:45:49,939
I put my wife through hell

372
00:45:52,567 --> 00:45:55,195
and screwed up as a detective...

373
00:45:59,949 --> 00:46:02,911
It's my fault this happened to her.

374
00:46:06,081 --> 00:46:08,083
So I've got to save her.

375
00:46:11,419 --> 00:46:15,173
If you save your wife, my daughter will die.

376
00:46:15,507 --> 00:46:17,675
I'll save your daughter, too.

377
00:46:20,220 --> 00:46:23,181
I still don't know if I can trust you.

378
00:46:28,937 --> 00:46:31,356
If I ever double-cross you...

379
00:46:33,983 --> 00:46:41,074
then... kill me and complete your mission.

380
00:46:57,298 --> 00:46:58,883
What will you do next?

381
00:47:01,344 --> 00:47:02,830
I'll meet the other players.

382
00:47:04,889 --> 00:47:06,583
Find the common factors.

383
00:47:09,686 --> 00:47:11,646
Taipei's a good start.

384
00:47:12,772 --> 00:47:14,774
Taipei? Why?

385
00:47:15,733 --> 00:47:19,195
I have a feeling I've met her before.

386
00:47:20,321 --> 00:47:22,282
The hostage's wife.

387
00:47:22,407 --> 00:47:23,366
TAIPEI

388
00:47:39,924 --> 00:47:42,135
Are you in the kiDnap GAME?

389
00:47:43,761 --> 00:47:45,263
What do you mean...?

390
00:47:46,097 --> 00:47:48,984
Don't keep secrets. Dad's life is at stake.

391
00:47:51,019 --> 00:47:52,550
I'm not keeping secrets.

392
00:47:55,356 --> 00:47:56,608
Liar.

393
00:48:00,820 --> 00:48:05,158
Where... When... I don't know.

394
00:48:07,118 --> 00:48:09,287
But I know her face.

395
00:48:11,873 --> 00:48:14,918
That's the first link between the players.

396
00:48:18,463 --> 00:48:19,476
Come with me.

397
00:48:23,134 --> 00:48:24,383
Let me think about it.

398
00:48:29,182 --> 00:48:30,558
All right.

399
00:48:33,353 --> 00:48:35,410
I'll fly to Taipei in the morning.

400
00:48:37,232 --> 00:48:38,729
Come when you've decided.

401
00:51:40,748 --> 00:51:43,042
My Dear Ayun. I'm sorry.

402
00:51:44,419 --> 00:51:47,755
I can't bring myself to kill.

403
00:51:49,674 --> 00:51:54,137
The rules of the game allow
only one to survive.

404
00:51:55,680 --> 00:51:57,724
If I kill someone,

405
00:51:58,766 --> 00:52:02,186
every hostage except Rian dies.

406
00:52:03,688 --> 00:52:09,735
As a father, I know it's right
to save her at any cost.

407
00:52:09,861 --> 00:52:10,987
But

408
00:52:13,030 --> 00:52:15,158
I'm not capable of murder.

409
00:52:27,587 --> 00:52:28,588
I'm waiting.

410
00:52:31,007 --> 00:52:32,175
Hopefully...

411
00:52:33,301 --> 00:52:34,761
he'll show up.

412
00:52:36,137 --> 00:52:37,430
If he doesn't?

413
00:52:38,514 --> 00:52:39,974
Then I'll go alone.

414
00:52:41,142 --> 00:52:43,535
I need to put a stop to this game.

415
00:52:45,605 --> 00:52:48,816
Think how it tormented the man in Manila

416
00:52:49,484 --> 00:52:52,528
and the woman in Bangkok.

417
00:52:55,948 --> 00:52:58,868
How it nearly drove Kiju to suicide.

418
00:53:03,998 --> 00:53:05,333
I know.

419
00:53:06,209 --> 00:53:12,465
This is the final boarding call for Flight 4321 to Taipei...

420
00:53:13,049 --> 00:53:14,884
Guess he's not coming.

421
00:53:15,384 --> 00:53:16,802
Take care.

422
00:53:16,928 --> 00:53:17,970
I will.

423
00:53:35,655 --> 00:53:37,323
Wait!

424
00:53:52,922 --> 00:53:54,173
That's why...

425
00:53:55,424 --> 00:53:57,260
I'm going to save Rian.

426
00:53:59,470 --> 00:54:03,850
We'll save the other hostages
and end the game.

427
00:54:07,520 --> 00:54:11,774
So we can see Rian in joy.

428
00:54:13,442 --> 00:54:19,657
So we can be a family of three again.

429
00:54:59,822 --> 00:55:01,449
Thanks for coming.

430
00:55:02,783 --> 00:55:03,951
It's nothing.

431
00:55:06,203 --> 00:55:07,705
One condition...

432
00:55:09,874 --> 00:55:14,378
If you double-cross me,
I will absolutely kill you.

433
00:55:16,589 --> 00:55:20,217
If I do, then kill me. But...

434
00:55:22,094 --> 00:55:24,221
that's not going to happen.

435
00:55:29,518 --> 00:55:35,045
I can't just take your word for it.

436
00:55:37,693 --> 00:55:41,240
But I want to believe in your ideals.

437
00:55:42,156 --> 00:55:45,346
So I'll go with you.

438
00:55:52,375 --> 00:55:53,108
Thanks.

439
00:56:10,559 --> 00:56:17,108
"What are you prioritizing
over the lives of your loved ones?

440
00:56:18,859 --> 00:56:25,658
"You are on a fool's errand...
Carry out your missions immediately."

441
00:56:45,177 --> 00:56:46,011
We have to go.

442
00:57:04,632 --> 00:57:08,381
5 DAYS AND 11 HOURS UNTIL THE GAME ENDS.
